/-!
# Cohomological descent along an fppf hypercovering of algebraic spaces

Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S` and `a : U → X` an fppf hypercovering of `X`
by a simplicial algebraic space (Section 0DH4), with the morphism of topoi
`a : Sh(U_étale) → Sh(X_étale)` of Section 0DE7. This file proves that for every
`K ∈ D⁺(X_étale)` the canonical map

`K → Ra_*(a⁻¹K)`

is an isomorphism, which is the content of Stacks 0DH7.

## The proof

This is the proof of the source. Consider the commutative diagram of topoi of Stacks 0DH5
```
Sh((Spaces/U)_{fppf, total}) --h--> Sh(U_étale)
        | a_fppf                       | a
Sh((Spaces/X)_fppf)        --h₋₁--> Sh(X_étale)
```
where `h` and `h₋₁` are given by the inclusions `V/U_n ↦ V/U_n` and `W ↦ W/X` of objects étale
over `U_n`, respectively `X`; it is the square of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.phComparisonSquareInverseImageIso` for the fppf topology. For an abelian
sheaf `F` on `X_étale`:

* the units of `h₋₁` and of every `h_{U_n}` are invertible and `h₋₁⁻¹F` is acyclic for `h₋₁,*`
  (Stacks 0DGF, through `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fppfSpacesEtaleAcyclic_of_algebraicSpace`);
  hence the unit of `h` is invertible, and `a_fppf⁻¹h₋₁⁻¹F` is acyclic for `h_*`, restriction to
  a simplicial degree `n` carrying it to `h_{U_n}⁻¹` of a sheaf on `U_{n, étale}` through the
  base change square `f_{small,*} ∘ h_{U_n,*} = h_{X,*} ∘ f_{big,*}` of `f : U_n → X`;
* `U` is a hypercovering of `X` in `(Spaces/S)_fppf` (Stacks 09X8), so the unit of `a_fppf` is
  invertible and `a_fppf⁻¹N` is acyclic for `a_{fppf,*}` (Stacks 0DA8, Stacks 0D8N).

Chasing around the square (`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.isIso_unit_app_of_comp_iso`,
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.isZero_rightDerived_of_comp_iso`) the unit `F → a_*a⁻¹F` is invertible
and `a⁻¹F` is acyclic for `a_*`; this is `Ra_*a⁻¹ = Rh₋₁,* Ra_{fppf,*} a_fppf⁻¹ h₋₁⁻¹ = id` on a
single sheaf. Leray's acyclicity lemma gives the statement on `D⁺`
(`Stacks.ComparingTopologies.isIso_derivedPlusAdjunction_unit_app`).

## Main results

In the namespace `AlgebraicGeometry.Space`:

* `IsFppfHypercovering.isIso_etaleAugmentation_abelianUnit_app`: the unit `F → a_*a⁻¹F` is
  invertible on abelian sheaves.
* `IsFppfHypercovering.isZero_rightDerived_etaleAugmentation`: `R^q a_*(a⁻¹F) = 0` for `q > 0`.
* `IsFppfHypercovering.isIso_abelianTotalAdjunction_rightDerivedFunctorPlus_unit_app`:
  `K → Ra_*(a⁻¹K)` is an isomorphism for `K ∈ D⁺(X_étale)`, in any model of the derived
  categories.

## Implementation notes

`X_étale` is the spaces-étale site of `X`, which Section 0DE7 identifies with the small étale site.
The fppf site of algebraic spaces is the one whose topology is generated by all fppf coverings
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fppfTopology`); Stacks 0DGF is available for a big fppf site of algebraic
spaces in the sense of Stacks 0DBV, whose topology is shown to be the same.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DH7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DH7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DH5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DH5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGG)
